{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>At the turn of morning.</b> Close to morning." "<b>To its strength.</b> To its force, and it is a noun, like נהרות איתן (Psalms 74:15)." "<b>Went toward it.</b> I explained it: they think in their going that they are returning to dry land, yet they went toward it. One should laugh at Hivi the Kenite's bones, who said that Moses knew the time of the sea's ebb at its descent and the time of its rise at its going out, and he passed through with it at the ebbing of the waters as is its custom, and Pharaoh did not know the sea's custom, therefore he drowned. And these are words of madness, for by the sea's custom at its ebb no place dries up and walls of water remain on its right and left, for all dries up; and furthermore, the end of the sea's descent and the beginning of its rise cannot be determined except after hours; and furthermore, Israel had not finished crossing until Pharaoh and his army drowned." "<b>And YHWH shook off.</b> From the heavy stem, and close to it is also חצני נערתי (Nehemiah 5:13), in the manner of רמה בים (below, 15:1)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {2 "Reading ישתחקו as from root שחק 'to laugh'; text could also be pointed as ישתחוו 'they will bow,' but context favors the former."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:34.498904639Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}